{"seq":2,"slug":"kinds-of-docs-that-help","title":"Kinds Of Docs That Help","docCount":3,"url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/kinds-of-docs-that-help","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"readme-as-entry-point","title":"README 作为入口","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/kinds-of-docs-that-help/readme-as-entry-point","wordCount":2342,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"adrs-and-decision-records","title":"ADR 与决策记录","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/kinds-of-docs-that-help/adrs-and-decision-records","wordCount":2136,"readingTime":9},{"seq":3,"slug":"inline-docs-and-comments","title":"内联文档与注释","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-friendly-documentation/kinds-of-docs-that-help/inline-docs-and-comments","wordCount":1903,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲几类对 agent(和人)最有用的文档,各自该怎么用好。README 是项目的入口文档——agent 进项目先读它搞清这是什么、怎么装跑、怎么用,它该简洁、准确、把最该知道的放最前。ADR(架构决策记录)记下\"为什么这么设计\"——把决策的背景、选项、取舍写下来,让 agent 理解约束、不好心改坏重要决策,这是代码本身最读不出的知识。内联文档与注释贴在代码旁,解释难懂的一段\"为什么这么写\"——注释该解释意图和原因(代码说不清的),而非复述代码做了什么;好注释帮 agent 读懂难点,废注释和过期注释反而添乱。\n"}